nodecode-by2kb is a rewrite of Charlesmpc's Charlesmpc/by2kb:

  https://github.com/Charlesmpc/by2kb
  commit 5983ca8a479feb87321f5c37f59cf8ae28818451
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Charles (LICENSE)

The rewrite is by2kb/integrations/hermes, the plugin's Hermes gateway
integration, as a Nodecode cell. What it keeps: the verbs the plugin ran
through `by2kb` -- `search discover`, `search latest`, `search select` with
the external-agent enricher, `ingest`, and the staged `enrichment next` /
`enrichment submit` pair -- with the same argv, the same JSON read the same
way, the same allowed exit codes (0 and 1 for a search, 0 and 4 for an
ingest, 0..4 for a selection), the same three artifacts reported by the same
names (raw_md, abstract_md, updated_md), the abstract shown without its
front matter, and the same staging rule: a job whose summaries are pending
says which job to carry on with. The scope the plugin derived from platform,
chat and user is derived here from the session, so a conversation's
recommendation list answers its own numbers and no other conversation's.
The plugin's standing guidance became the cell's help topic and one
paragraph in the harness sections every request carries.

What is left out: the gateway hook. In Hermes a message that held a video
URL, a `by2kb TOPIC` prefix or a bare number was intercepted before the
model saw it; Nodecode has no such seam, so the model calls the tools and
`/by2kb` gives the operator the same three routes. The plugin's Chinese
chat replies, its 512-operation enrichment loop over a host model, and its
Hermes skill files are gone with it: the staged operations are answered by
the session's own model through by2kb_next and by2kb_submit, one operation
at a time, as the plugin's own manual-enrichment path described.

Nothing of the original's Python is bundled. The cell runs the same by2kb
program the plugin ran, on PATH, and its own code is Common Lisp.
